      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the commit message say what fails without the patch? As far as I can see, in a 4KB process: `mmap()` of a (1 + 2^n) × 4KB ring fails with `-EINVAL`, `PERF_RECORD_MMAP` offsets miss the 4KB slice, and sampled page sizes are the kernel\u0027s (16KB for a 4KB page).\n\nIt would also help to say that the data PTEs don\u0027t follow `vma_slice_offset()`, and why that\u0027s fine. I think it is here: the VMA is `VM_PFNMAP | VM_IO` with no `-\u003eaccess`, so GUP, `__access_remote_vm()` and coredumps never read through these PTEs.\n\nAlso, could the subject say \"4KB processes\" rather than \"4K process\", as in the rest of the series?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "fcddcede99bd82769c30134512e2e92f7d3170f8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4b2c5f77_059ceab6",
        "filename": "kernel/events/core.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 6889,
