        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T21:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the 4KB layout stays, would you mind moving this mapping out of `kernel/events/core.c`? It\u0027s about 45 lines of P3S-only code, plus the `#ifdef`ed fields and accessors in `internal.h`. A P3S header that kernel/events includes (e.g. `include/linux/p3s/perf.h`) could hold it, with a one-line dispatch left in `map_range()`.\n\nCould the new names also say P3S rather than PPPS, the old abbreviation (`perf_map_main_ppps()`, `perf_map_aux_ppps()`)?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "fcddcede99bd82769c30134512e2e92f7d3170f8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9fad7045_5fd0e1e8",
        "filename": "kernel/events/core.c",
